From: Isaac Connor <connortechnology@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] vf_drawtext_ni: build the overlay frame pool in the
 in-place path

Against Quadra V5.8.0 (libxcoder 5806tCr2).

init_hwframe_uploader() builds the output frame pool for s->api_ctx only
under "if (s->use_watermark)". The in-place path needs one just as much:
both paths reach ni_device_alloc_frame() with NI_SCALER_FLAG_IO set in
filter_frame(), so both take an output frame from that session for every
input frame. Without the pool, ni_scaler_session_read_hwdesc() gets
frame index 0 -- "2D could not acquire frame" -- and spins its for(;;)
up to 1000 times, issuing an INST_BUF_INFO_RW_UPLOAD device query on
each pass.

The crop session does get a pool, but sized 1, which allows exactly one
frame in flight: the next input waits for the previous crop output to be
recycled, in the same spin.

Measured on a ZoneMinder capture process, one Quadra, 3840x2160 h264
decode to hardware frames, drawing one or two labels per frame through
drawtext with drawbox ahead of it:

  Annotation over 100 detections (hardware filters): drawbox 5.96ms
  each, drawtext 76 calls mean 2691.77ms max 17469.20ms, 20 blocked
  over 250ms

  drawtext calls                 76
  under 250ms                    56
  blocked 6.21 - 6.45s            9
  blocked 11.46 - 17.47s         11

With the patch, same monitor, same workload:

  Annotation over 100 detections (hardware filters): drawbox 5.12ms
  each, drawtext 99 calls mean 6.85ms max 15.86ms, 0 blocked over
  250ms

  drawtext calls                 99
  under 250ms                    99
  blocked                         0

Mean 2691.77ms to 6.85ms, worst case 17469.20ms to 15.86ms, and no
stall at all. drawtext now costs about what drawbox costs, which is
what it should: the filter was never slow, it was waiting.

26% of calls stalled before. The two clusters are one and two exhausted
retry loops, the crop session and the overlay session starving
separately or together. Identical work in the fast and slow cases -- the same one or
two short labels -- so this is a wait for a frame, not drawing cost.
vf_drawbox_ni.c in the same graph, over the same frames, builds its
pool unconditionally and never blocks once: 90 calls, 5.96ms mean,
10ms worst case.

Build the overlay pool unconditionally at DEFAULT_NI_FILTER_POOL_SIZE
plus extra_hw_frames, as vf_drawbox_ni.c does, and give the crop session
the same size.

--- a/libavfilter/vf_drawtext_ni.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_drawtext_ni.c
@@ -2455,6 +2455,7 @@
                                  AVFrame *frame, int txt_w, int txt_h)
 {
     int ret;
+    int pool_size;
     AVHWFramesContext *hwframe_ctx;
     AVHWFramesContext *out_frames_ctx;
     AVHWFramesContext *main_frame_ctx;
@@ -2547,17 +2548,26 @@
 #if IS_FFMPEG_61_AND_ABOVE
     s->buffer_limit = 1;
 #endif
-    if (s->use_watermark) {
-        // init the out pool for the overlay session when use watermark
-        ret = ff_ni_build_frame_pool(&s->api_ctx, frame->width, frame->height,
-                                        main_frame_ctx->sw_format, 4,
-                                        s->buffer_limit);
+    /* The overlay session allocates an output frame for every input frame,
+     * in the watermark path and the in-place path alike: both reach
+     * ni_device_alloc_frame() with NI_SCALER_FLAG_IO set. Build the pool
+     * unconditionally, as vf_drawbox_ni.c does. Built only for
+     * use_watermark, the in-place path had no pool of its own, and
+     * ni_scaler_session_read_hwdesc() returned frame index 0 and spun --
+     * 1000 retries, each issuing a device query, before giving up.
+     */
+    pool_size = DEFAULT_NI_FILTER_POOL_SIZE;
+#if IS_FFMPEG_71_AND_ABOVE
+    pool_size += ctx->extra_hw_frames > 0 ? ctx->extra_hw_frames : 0;
+#endif
+    ret = ff_ni_build_frame_pool(&s->api_ctx, frame->width, frame->height,
+                                 main_frame_ctx->sw_format, pool_size,
+                                 s->buffer_limit);
 
-        if (ret < 0) {
-            av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR,
-                    "Internal output allocation failed rc = %d\n", ret);
-            return ret;
-        }
+    if (ret < 0) {
+        av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR,
+                "Internal output allocation failed rc = %d\n", ret);
+        return ret;
     }
 
     // if background frame has no alpha, set up an extra intermediate scaler
@@ -2592,8 +2602,12 @@
         s->crop_session_opened = 1;
 
         // init the out pool for the crop session, make it rgba
+        /* One frame is one frame in flight: the next input has to wait for
+         * the last crop output to be recycled, and waits in the same
+         * 1000-retry spin. Size it like every other filter's pool.
+         */
         ret = ff_ni_build_frame_pool(&s->crop_api_ctx, txt_w, txt_h,
-                                     AV_PIX_FMT_RGBA, 1, 0);
+                                     AV_PIX_FMT_RGBA, pool_size, 0);
 
         if (ret < 0) {
             av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR,
